course: dictionary
lesson: 9334
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Spindle is a good example. Read the sentence first, then choose the meaning that fits the clues. «Then she lets him play a string game with the spindle-whorl until the Baby laughs and falls asleep.» String and spinning are the clues, so the spindle here is the thin stick used for spinning thread.
explain: The first meaning is a thin, pointed stick that people used long ago to twist wool or other fibres into thread. «A spindle whorl is a small weight of clay or stone on a stick, used for spinning thread for thousands of years.» The weight helps the stick turn.
explain: The second meaning is a rod or pin in a machine that turns round, or something turns around. In science and DT, a spindle is a turning part. The third meaning is spindly, the adjective form, which means long and thin, like «spindly legs».
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does the sentence still make sense? If it does, you have chosen well.
fact: A spindle is a thin, pointed stick used to twist fibres into thread.
fact: «A spindle whorl is a small weight of clay or stone on a stick» helped people spin thread for thousands of years.
fact: The spinning-wheel was invented much later than the spindle, about a thousand years ago.
fact: In machines, a spindle is a rod or pin that turns round.
fact: «Spindly» means long and thin, and a «spindle tree» is a hedgerow tree whose wood was used for spindles.
exercise: «Then she lets him play a string game with the spindle-whorl until the Baby laughs.» In this sentence, what is a spindle-whorl? | A bell that rings when you pull a string | A rod that holds a door open | *A small weight of clay or stone on a stick, used for spinning | A tree growing in a hedgerow
exercise: Mia reads «The spindle turned faster and faster inside the machine.» What does spindle mean here? | *A rod or pin in a machine that turns round | A thin, pointed stick for spinning wool | A long, thin leg | A princess in a fairy tale
exercise: Which word describes something long and thin, like «spindly legs»? | *spindly | spooky | spindle-whorl | spinning
test: In the fairy tale Sleeping Beauty, what happens when the princess pricks her finger on a spindle? | She starts to sing | She is crowned queen | She turns into a bird | *She falls asleep for a hundred years
test: Which word fits the gap? «The thin, pointed ___ was used to twist wool into thread.» | *spindle | hedge | machine | bell
exam: Which meaning of spindle fits best in «The spindle of the old machine began to squeak as it turned round»? | *A rod in a machine that turns round | A thin stick for spinning thread | A long, thin leg | A princess in a fairy tale
